<h2>Wax Prints — shapes, fabric area and ribbon perimeter</h2>
<p><a href="https://cms-assets.illustrativemathematics.org/bch5lt3iffuoihcxjzyjphgijuno" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original 2021 four-page student tasks</a>. Examine the original textile photo with your teacher.</p>
<p>Design on grid paper: one <strong>rhombus, rectangle or square</strong>, and one <strong>different quadrilateral</strong> which is none of those. Repeat <strong>each at least five times</strong> and color your pattern. Teacher inspects the actual drawing.</p>
<p>For Activity 2, the teacher gives Problem Card and Data Card separately to partners. Ask why the measurement is needed before exchanging information. Solve two rounds and swap roles. Hidden source card measurements and answers are intentionally not displayed here.</p>
<p>Area measures fabric using square feet; border ribbon uses feet of perimeter, plus any separate edge specified by the original task. Original gated Cool-down remains teacher-access only.</p>
